{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":95575,"duration_api_ms":95232,"num_turns":4,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6f05ab70-947b-4276-89f3-ba01a9f92e43","total_cost_usd":0.41568665000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27871,"cache_read_input_tokens":113651,"output_tokens":994,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27871,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":994,"cacheReadInputTokens":113651,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27871,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.25589425,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":120,"outputTokens":5874,"cacheReadInputTokens":789949,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41046,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.15979240000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept the chemistry-stress assertion consistency amendment; reject the carbonate-equilibrium throttling amendment. The first addresses a real doc/assertion mismatch where the probe's narrative promises molt failures but the code no longer checks for them. The second proposes optimizing a closed-form quadratic solver that is already gated behind Verbosity::Trace — there's no demonstrated bottleneck and reducing cadence would degrade trace fidelity.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-4ed757e6","decision":"accept","rationale":"The doc comment on the chemistry stress probe (lines 616-625) explicitly states the scenario should produce 'molt failures, increased mortality, condition decline'. However, the current assertions only verify mortality, elevated molt_stress_index > 0.2, and condition decline — the removed check that verified molt_failures > 0 or failed_molt_accum > 0 leaves a gap where the probe can pass green even if the model produces zero molt failures. This is a real test-vs-documentation inconsistency. The amendment's suggested remedies are both sound: either restore a directional assertion (possibly softened to check molt_stress OR failed_molt_accum > 0) or update the doc comment to remove the molt-failures claim. Either way the current state is a defect — the probe's narrative contract is not enforced by its assertions."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-f7d31042","decision":"reject","rationale":"The performance concern is speculative and unsupported by the implementation. First, emit_tick_snapshot already exits early unless stage_trace.is_enabled(), which is only true at Verbosity::Trace — the highest verbosity level, explicitly opt-in for diagnostic use. Second, solve_carbonate_equilibrium is a closed-form quadratic solve (a·H² + b·H + c = 0 with early-return fast paths for negligible DIC/alkalinity) — not an iterative numerical method. A single quadratic formula evaluation per tick is negligible even over 1500 ticks. Third, reducing the call to daily-only ticks would make the tick_snapshot trace inconsistent: consumers expecting per-tick carbonate data would get gaps, undermining the trace's purpose. Without profiling evidence of an actual bottleneck, this optimization trades trace fidelity for no demonstrated gain."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"42c62d87-e4c8-411b-9bb6-9559d69921e4"}
